OL,3,GNEWSAWhy is the hosepipe ban still in
OL,4,Aplace?
OL,5,
OL,6,FWater companies say that while
OL,7,Fhouseholds are using less water now,
OL,8,Fthe hosepipe ban is staying in place.
OL,10,FWessex Water and Bristol Water
OL,11,Fintroduced a hosepipe ban last month,
OL,12,Fthe first since the famous summer of
OL,13,F1976, after seeing exceptionally high
OL,14,Fdemand on their networks over a
OL,15,Fprolonged period.
OL,17,FBut why is the ban still in place even
OL,18,Fafter we have seen some rainfall in the
OL,19,Farea?
OL,21,FWe have put together all the
OL,22,Finformation you need.
OL,23,APub: 24-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
